# Environment Setup

## Requirements

- **Node.js** `>= 22.22` (required by `@lobehub/docs-kit`; the repo has no `.nvmrc`).
- **pnpm** `10.20.0` (`packageManager` in `package.json`).
- No lockfile: `.npmrc` sets `lockfile=false`; do not commit one.

## Install

```bash
pnpm install
```

`pnpm install` also runs:

- `postinstall` → `scripts/postinstall-lexical-patch.cjs` (patches the Lexical Yjs build in
  `node_modules`).
- `prepare` → `husky` (git hooks) and `npm run setup` (`lobedocs typegen`, docs type
  generation).

If `pnpm type-check` reports missing exports from dependencies (e.g. `@lobehub/ui`), your
`node_modules` is stale: run `pnpm install` again.

## Common Scripts

```bash
pnpm dev                 # docs site with live demos (lobedocs dev); same as docs:dev / start
pnpm docs:build          # static docs build + docs validations
pnpm build               # library build (tsdown); build:watch for watch mode
pnpm test                # vitest (watch); `pnpm vitest run` for a single run
pnpm test:coverage       # vitest run --coverage
pnpm type-check          # tsc --noEmit
pnpm lint                # eslint --fix on src and tests
pnpm lint:style          # stylelint --fix
pnpm lint:md             # remark lint for Markdown
pnpm lint:circular       # dpdm circular-import check
pnpm ci                  # lint:circular + lint + type-check
pnpm demo:yjs-server     # local Yjs collaboration demo server (YJS_DEMO_PORT, default 12345)
```

`scripts/yjs-websocket-demo-server.md` documents the collaboration demo server.

## Git Hooks

`.husky/pre-commit` runs `type-check` (skipped when `CI=true`), `lint:circular` and
`lint-staged`:

- `*.{md,mdc}`: `remark --output` (config `.remarkrc.mjs`) then Prettier.
- `*.json`: Prettier.
- `*.{js,jsx}` and `*.{ts,tsx}`: Prettier, Stylelint, ESLint.
- `*.{mjs,cjs}`: Prettier, ESLint.

`.husky/commit-msg` runs commitlint (gitmoji + Conventional Commits). Do not bypass hooks
with `--no-verify`.

## Debug Logging

Logging uses the `debug` package (see [debug-logging](mdc:.cursor/rules/debug-logging.mdc)).

```bash
# Node: tests, headless editor, scripts (.env.example contains DEBUG="lobe-editor:*")
DEBUG=lobe-editor:* pnpm vitest run src/plugins/markdown
```

```javascript
// Browser (docs dev server or a host app)
localStorage.debug = 'lobe-editor:*'; // reload afterwards
// or, from code
import { browserDebug } from '@/utils/debug';
browserDebug.enable('lobe-editor:kernel,lobe-editor:plugin:*');
```

`isDev` / `devConsole` in `src/utils/debug.ts` only check `process.env.NODE_ENV ===
'development'`.

## Hot Reload Mode

When hot reload mode is on, the kernel lets plugins, services and decorators be registered again
(with a warning) instead of throwing, which keeps HMR working.

- Each `Kernel` detects it on creation: the global override if set, otherwise
  `NODE_ENV === 'development'`, webpack / Vite / Next.js dev markers, or a `localhost`,
  `127.0.0.1` or `*.local` hostname.
- Force it for all instances from the app entry:

```typescript
import { disableHotReload, enableHotReload } from '@lobehub/editor';

enableHotReload(); // Kernel.setGlobalHotReloadMode(true)
disableHotReload(); // Kernel.setGlobalHotReloadMode(false)
```

- Per instance: `kernel.setHotReloadMode(enabled)` / `kernel.isHotReloadMode()`;
  `Kernel.resetGlobalHotReloadMode()` returns to automatic detection.

## Tests

`vitest.config.ts`: `jsdom` environment, `globals: true`, aliases `@` and `@lobehub/editor`
to `src/`, and inlines `@lobehub/ui` and `@lexical/*`. There is no global setup file. Coverage
thresholds apply to `src/common` and `src/editor-kernel`.
